{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "frankendom-v3 data/physics.json (states.death, kill, motorTuning, bones) + data/hero-death.json (ragdoll); body parts follow the 20-part role table of physics.json 'bones'",
  "about": "Death-only ragdoll for the Mixamo-rigged fighters (V3_TO_UNITY rows 3, 4, 8). ON since 2026-11-04 (Dom: Dracula lay flat like a board with the death clip held); set enabled false to restore the held death clip. Only the fighter that is killed is converted; nameContains [] = both. Presentation only: the sim never reads it. Spring/damper numbers are PhysX starting points to tune in the player (V3's Jolt motor gain/damping are relative multipliers here). PHYS1 v1 (2026-11-05): rig pre-built at scene load (kinematic, Hurtbox-layer trigger capsules), velocities inherited at death, blow impulse along the attacker's facing split over zone / spine2 / hips, V3 role-table joint limits (spine 20/15, spine1+2 18/12, neck 50/60, head 55/70, arm 150/100, hand 80/70, thigh 85/45, foot 40/20, forearm hinge -30..150, shin hinge -3.2..136.8), the 5 rigid cape / skirt bodies removed (their bones carry no skin weight). Hinge: min..max degrees about the axis found from the rest pose (bend +1 = toward the fighter's forward, -1 = backward); enabled:false falls back to swing / twist.",
